USER     def withFilter(q: T => Boolean): WithFilter^{Try.this, p, q}                   = new WithFilter(x => p(x) && q(x))
USER   }
USER   
USER 
USER   /** Applies the given function `f` if this is a `Failure`, otherwise returns this if this is a `Success`.
USER    *  This is like `flatMap` for the exception.
USER    *
USER    *  @tparam U the type of the value in the resulting `Try`, a supertype of `T`
USER    *  @param pf the partial function to apply if this is a `Failure`
USER    *  @return the `Try` produced by applying `pf` to the exception if this is a `Failure` and `pf` is defined for it, this `Failure` unchanged if `pf` is not defined for the exception, or this `Success` unchanged; any non-fatal exception thrown by `pf` is caught and returned as a `Failure`
