USER THE DESCRIPTION (whole-comment placeholder) — this needs judgment.
USER These rules follow the official Scala style guide (https://docs.scala-lang.org/style/scaladoc.html):
USER - Write a first sentence that stands alone as the API-index summary of what
USER   this declaration is or does. It must make sense read by itself. Get to the point
USER   as quickly as possible.
USER - VOICE: declarative, third person, present tense — document what the code DOES, not
USER   what it should do ("Returns the result of applying `f`", not "Return ..." or
USER   "Should return ..."). For a method/def, start with a third-person verb ("Returns ...",
USER   "Creates ...", "Validates ..."). For a class/trait/object, a noun phrase
USER   ("A `Source` backed by ...") or a verb phrase ("Provides ...") both read well.
USER - NO SELF-REFERENCE: do not begin with "This class/trait/object/method ...". Describe
USER   the thing directly (the style guide prefers "Does XXX" over "This class does XXX").
USER - Add further sentences only when they convey non-obvious behavior, constraints,
USER   side effects, or usage. For a trivial accessor, one sentence is the whole doc.
USER - Do NOT restate the signature ("a method that takes an Int and returns a String").
USER - Match the voice and altitude of nearby Scaladoc in the same file.
USER - HONESTY OVER CONFIDENCE: if the code does not let you determine the intended
USER   meaning, write your best-guess description AND append on its own line, inside
USER   the comment, a marker: `@note NEEDS-HUMAN: <the specific question you could not
USER   resolve>`. A flagged honest guess is far more useful than a confident wrong doc.
USER 
USER TAGS:
USER - @param: purpose of the parameter; constraints (non-negative, non-null), units
USER   (ms, bytes), defaults — only what is true per the code.
USER - @tparam: what the type parameter represents and any bounds.
USER - @return: first decide whether to KEEP or DROP it, using the project's redundant-@return
USER   rule (same as remove-redundant-returns):
USER   * DROP it (delete the whole `@return TODO FILL IN` line) ONLY when BOTH hold:
USER     (a) the comment's description (the prose before the tags) BEGINS with the word
USER         "Returns" — whether that description already existed or you just wrote it, AND
USER     (b) that description already fully states what is returned, so an @return would only
USER         restate it and add no edge case, sentinel, unit, bound, or guarantee.
USER     The very first word of the description must be exactly "Returns". If it begins with any
USER     other word ("Creates", "Computes", "Gets", "A", ...), KEEP the @return.
USER     When you delete the tag, also delete an orphaned blank ` *` line if removing the tag
